## Core Logic

The purpose of this project is to accelerate the HNSW proximity graph vector index construction with GPU. The core idea is reflected in @kernel.cuh and @kernel.cu, particularly the `build_graph_kernel` function.

Here is its main logic:

1. compute the distances between new batch with a middle level of old of a moderate size; compute the distances between new vectors for future use
2. connect new vectors to old vectors as well as add the reverse edges starting from the middle level to the upper-most level of each new vector
3. search for old vectors in the lower levels starting from the middle level, connect new to old as well as add the reverse edges during the process
4. prune for new vectors on each level, taking into consideration the old vectors already connected as well as the new vectors inserted
5. prune for the old vectors
6. move on to next batch of new vectors